---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'quick-run', text: 'Quick Run with Docker' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'compose', text: 'Docker Compose Setup' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'air-gapped-isolation', text: 'Air-Gapped Container Hardening' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Docker & Air-Gapped Setup"
  description="How to deploy Binsight inside secure Docker containers and isolated offline networks."
  currentSlug="docker"
  headings={headings}
>
  <p>
    Binsight is published to the GitHub Container Registry as <code>ghcr.io/adrijshikhar/binsight:latest</code> with multi-architecture support for <code>linux/amd64</code> and <code>linux/arm64</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="quick-run">Quick Run with Docker</h2>
  <p>
    Mount your binlog directory as a read-only volume and expose port <code>8080</code>:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`docker run -d \\
  --name binsight \\
  -p 8080:8080 \\
  -v /var/log/mysql:/binlogs:ro \\
  -v binsight-state:/var/lib/binsight \\
  ghcr.io/adrijshikhar/binsight:latest /binlogs`}
    lang="bash"
    title="Terminal"
  />

  <h2 id="compose">Docker Compose Setup</h2>
  <p>
    For long-running staging environments or shared forensic workstations, define a <code>docker-compose.yml</code>:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`version: '3.8'

services:
  binsight:
    image: ghcr.io/adrijshikhar/binsight:latest
    container_name: binsight
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"
    environment:
      - BINSIGHT_BIND=0.0.0.0
      - BINSIGHT_PORT=8080
      - BINSIGHT_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/binsight
    volumes:
      # Mount binlogs strictly read-only (:ro)
      - /data/mysql-binlogs:/binlogs:ro
      # Persist SQLite index cache across container restarts
      - binsight-state:/var/lib/binsight
    command: ["/binlogs"]

volumes:
  binsight-state:`}
    lang="yaml"
    title="docker-compose.yml"
  />

  <h2 id="air-gapped-isolation">Air-Gapped Container Hardening</h2>
  <p>
    For defense, banking, or medical audits where zero outbound network access is permitted:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Disable Container Networking:</strong> If only reading local files on disk, pass <code>--network host</code> or attach only to an internal loopback network.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Read-Only Root Filesystem:</strong> Pass <code>--read-only</code> to Docker. Binsight only requires write access to the mounted state volume at <code>/var/lib/binsight</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Drop All Capabilities:</strong> Pass <code>--cap-drop=ALL</code>. Binsight runs as an unprivileged user and requires no Linux kernel capabilities.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`docker run --rm \\
  --cap-drop=ALL \\
  --read-only \\
  -p 127.0.0.1:8080:8080 \\
  -v /data/binlogs:/binlogs:ro \\
  -v /tmp/binsight-state:/var/lib/binsight \\
  ghcr.io/adrijshikhar/binsight:latest /binlogs`}
    lang="bash"
    title="Hardened Execution"
  />
</DocsLayout>
